(window.XZ_MANUAL_CHAPTERS=window.XZ_MANUAL_CHAPTERS||{})["performance"]="<header class=\"mc-head\"><p class=\"mc-eyebrow\">On the player<\/p><h2 class=\"mc-title\" tabindex=\"-1\">Beat jump and performance features<\/h2><p class=\"mc-lede\">Beat jump distances, gate cue, smart cue, key sync and RAM tracks.<\/p><p class=\"applies\" data-applies=\"both\">Applies to <b>MODERN and CLASSIC<\/b><\/p><\/header><p>XZ Mods adds performance features to the pads and deck keys: two pages of beat jump sizes you choose, gate cue, smart cue, key shift and KEY SYNC, and RAM tracks. Their settings live on one MODS page, PLAY. Every change saves to your USB as you make it.<\/p>\n<h3 id=\"m-the-play-page\" data-anchor=\"the-play-page\">The PLAY page<\/h3>\n<p>Open MODS and choose PLAY in the section rail.<\/p>\n<figure class=\"mf\" id=\"f-performance-1\"><div class=\"mf-frame\"><div class=\"mf-bar\"><span class=\"mf-label\">MODS · PLAY<\/span><\/div><div class=\"mf-stage\"><img src=\"manual/shots/6484ac8bf987a191.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"The PLAY page with the default settings: gate cue and smart cue off, the default jump sizes, and the rekordbox button above LINK on INTERFACE.\" data-iface=\"modern\"><img src=\"manual/shots/d59c5dd71f06b3fd.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"The PLAY page with the default settings: gate cue and smart cue off, the default jump sizes, and the rekordbox button above LINK on INTERFACE.\" data-iface=\"classic\"><span class=\"mf-spot\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span><div class=\"mf-marks\" role=\"group\" aria-label=\"Numbered points on the picture\"><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"1\" data-x=\"37.500\" data-y=\"17.500\" aria-label=\"1: BEAT JUMP PADS\" aria-describedby=\"f-performance-1-1\">1<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"2\" data-x=\"31.250\" data-y=\"27.500\" aria-label=\"2: GATE CUE\" aria-describedby=\"f-performance-1-2\">2<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"3\" data-x=\"75.000\" data-y=\"27.500\" aria-label=\"3: SMART CUE\" aria-describedby=\"f-performance-1-3\">3<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"4\" data-x=\"28.750\" data-y=\"40.833\" aria-label=\"4: KEYS\" aria-describedby=\"f-performance-1-4\">4<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"5\" data-x=\"75.625\" data-y=\"40.833\" aria-label=\"5: RAM TRACKS\" aria-describedby=\"f-performance-1-5\">5<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"6\" data-x=\"43.750\" data-y=\"54.167\" aria-label=\"6: REKORDBOX BUTTON\" aria-describedby=\"f-performance-1-6\">6<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"7\" data-x=\"25.000\" data-y=\"88.542\" aria-label=\"7: Dock\" aria-describedby=\"f-performance-1-7\">7<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"8\" data-x=\"89.750\" data-y=\"88.542\" aria-label=\"8: Works on\" aria-describedby=\"f-performance-1-8\">8<\/button><\/div><\/div><\/div><figcaption>The PLAY page with the default settings: gate cue and smart cue off, the default jump sizes, and the <span class=\"xzb\" data-key=\"rekordbox\"><img class=\"xzb-g\" src=\"assets/buttons/rekordbox.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"92.16\" height=\"32\"><span class=\"xzb-n\">rekordbox<\/span><\/span> button above <span class=\"xzb\" data-key=\"link\"><img class=\"xzb-g\" src=\"assets/buttons/link.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"54.02\" height=\"32\"><span class=\"xzb-n\">LINK<\/span><\/span> on INTERFACE.<\/figcaption><ol class=\"mf-legend\" aria-label=\"What the numbers show\"><li data-n=\"1\" id=\"f-performance-1-1\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">1<\/span><div><b>BEAT JUMP PADS<\/b> <span>Opens the beat jump editor. The numbers are your page 1 and page 2 sizes in beats.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"2\" id=\"f-performance-1-2\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">2<\/span><div><b>GATE CUE<\/b> <span>Hot cues play only while you hold the pad. Off by default.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"3\" id=\"f-performance-1-3\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">3<\/span><div><b>SMART CUE<\/b> <span>A hot cue press also moves the CUE point there. Off by default.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"4\" id=\"f-performance-1-4\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">4<\/span><div><b>KEYS<\/b> <span>Opens the key page: key shift and KEY SYNC for all four decks.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"5\" id=\"f-performance-1-5\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">5<\/span><div><b>RAM TRACKS<\/b> <span>Opens RAM TRACKS: copy a deck's track into memory.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"6\" id=\"f-performance-1-6\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">6<\/span><div><b>REKORDBOX BUTTON<\/b> <span>What the rekordbox button does, alone and with SHIFT. See Controls on the player.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"7\" id=\"f-performance-1-7\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">7<\/span><div><b>Dock<\/b> <span>Explains the highlighted row in plain words.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"8\" id=\"f-performance-1-8\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">8<\/span><div><b>Works on<\/b> <span>The decks the highlighted feature works on, in mixer order 3 1 2 4. A dim number is a deck it does not work on, with the reason below.<\/span><\/div><\/li><\/ol><\/figure>\n<p>If the cue engine has not reported on this USB loader, GATE CUE and SMART CUE show as SET UP GATE CUE and SET UP SMART CUE instead of switches. See <a class=\"m-link\" href=\"#manual\" data-chapter=\"performance\" data-anchor=\"feature-setup\">Feature setup<\/a>.<\/p>\n<h3 id=\"m-beat-jump\" data-anchor=\"beat-jump\">Beat jump<\/h3>\n<p>In BEAT JUMP mode the eight pads form four pairs: A/B, C/D, E/F and G/H. The first pad of a pair jumps back, the second jumps forward, by the same number of beats. With a loop on, the loop moves by that amount instead.<\/p>\n<p>You get two pages of sizes:<\/p>\n<div class=\"table\"><table><thead><tr><th>Page<\/th><th>How you select it<\/th><th>Default sizes A/B, C/D, E/F, G/H<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td>Page 1<\/td><td>Press <span class=\"xzb\" data-key=\"beat-jump\"><img class=\"xzb-g\" src=\"assets/buttons/beat-jump.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"96.53\" height=\"32\"><span class=\"xzb-n\">BEAT JUMP<\/span><\/span><\/td><td>1, 2, 4, 8 beats<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Page 2<\/td><td>Hold <span class=\"xzb\" data-key=\"shift\"><img class=\"xzb-g\" src=\"assets/buttons/shift.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"57\" height=\"32\"><span class=\"xzb-n\">SHIFT<\/span><\/span>, press <span class=\"xzb\" data-key=\"beat-jump\"><img class=\"xzb-g\" src=\"assets/buttons/beat-jump.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"96.53\" height=\"32\"><span class=\"xzb-n\">BEAT JUMP<\/span><\/span>, let go of <span class=\"xzb\" data-key=\"shift\"><img class=\"xzb-g\" src=\"assets/buttons/shift.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"57\" height=\"32\"><span class=\"xzb-n\">SHIFT<\/span><\/span><\/td><td>16, 32, 64, 128 beats (4, 8, 16, 32 bars)<\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div>\n<div class=\"mx\" data-mx=\"beat-jump\" data-mode=\"scenes\" role=\"group\" aria-label=\"Beat jump, page 1 and page 2\"><ol class=\"mx-scenes\"><li data-title=\"Page 1\"><b>Page 1<\/b> <span>Press <span class=\"xzb\" data-key=\"beat-jump\"><img class=\"xzb-g\" src=\"assets/buttons/beat-jump.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"96.53\" height=\"32\"><span class=\"xzb-n\">BEAT JUMP<\/span><\/span>. With the default sizes the pairs A/B, C/D, E/F and G/H jump 1, 2, 4 and 8 beats. The first pad of a pair jumps back, the second forward.<\/span><\/li><li data-title=\"Page 2\"><b>Page 2<\/b> <span>Hold <span class=\"xzb\" data-key=\"shift\"><img class=\"xzb-g\" src=\"assets/buttons/shift.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"57\" height=\"32\"><span class=\"xzb-n\">SHIFT<\/span><\/span>, press <span class=\"xzb\" data-key=\"beat-jump\"><img class=\"xzb-g\" src=\"assets/buttons/beat-jump.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"96.53\" height=\"32\"><span class=\"xzb-n\">BEAT JUMP<\/span><\/span>, let go of <span class=\"xzb\" data-key=\"shift\"><img class=\"xzb-g\" src=\"assets/buttons/shift.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"57\" height=\"32\"><span class=\"xzb-n\">SHIFT<\/span><\/span>. The pairs jump 16, 32, 64 and 128 beats, and the pads light warm red and amber.<\/span><\/li><li data-title=\"With a loop on\"><b>With a loop on<\/b> <span>With a loop on, the loop moves by the jump instead.<\/span><\/li><\/ol><\/div>\n<ol class=\"steps\"><li>Press <span class=\"xzb\" data-key=\"beat-jump\"><img class=\"xzb-g\" src=\"assets/buttons/beat-jump.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"96.53\" height=\"32\"><span class=\"xzb-n\">BEAT JUMP<\/span><\/span> for page 1, or <span class=\"xzb\" data-key=\"shift\"><img class=\"xzb-g\" src=\"assets/buttons/shift.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"57\" height=\"32\"><span class=\"xzb-n\">SHIFT<\/span><\/span> + <span class=\"xzb\" data-key=\"beat-jump\"><img class=\"xzb-g\" src=\"assets/buttons/beat-jump.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"96.53\" height=\"32\"><span class=\"xzb-n\">BEAT JUMP<\/span><\/span> for page 2.<\/li><li>Let go of <span class=\"xzb\" data-key=\"shift\"><img class=\"xzb-g\" src=\"assets/buttons/shift.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"57\" height=\"32\"><span class=\"xzb-n\">SHIFT<\/span><\/span>.<\/li><li>Press a pad. The first pad of a pair jumps back, the second forward.<\/li><\/ol>\n<p>Each deck remembers its own page. Choosing another pad mode and coming back with <span class=\"xzb\" data-key=\"beat-jump\"><img class=\"xzb-g\" src=\"assets/buttons/beat-jump.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"96.53\" height=\"32\"><span class=\"xzb-n\">BEAT JUMP<\/span><\/span> gives page 1 again. On page 2 the pads light warm red and amber, so you can see which page you are on. <span class=\"xzb\" data-key=\"shift\"><img class=\"xzb-g\" src=\"assets/buttons/shift.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"57\" height=\"32\"><span class=\"xzb-n\">SHIFT<\/span><\/span> + pad keeps its stock job on decks 1 and 2.<\/p>\n<h4 id=\"m-change-the-jump-sizes\" data-anchor=\"change-the-jump-sizes\">Change the jump sizes<\/h4>\n<p>Open MODS &gt; PLAY &gt; BEAT JUMP PADS. The editor shows the pads as they sit on the deck: A to D on top, E to H below.<\/p>\n<figure class=\"mf\" id=\"f-performance-2\"><div class=\"mf-frame\"><div class=\"mf-bar\"><span class=\"mf-label\">MODS · BEAT JUMP PADS<\/span><\/div><div class=\"mf-stage\"><img src=\"manual/shots/3af858dd88a5f69f.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"Editing page 2. Pads A and B are selected and jump 16 beats.\" data-iface=\"modern\"><img src=\"manual/shots/d1b8a865daaecb29.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"Editing page 2. Pads A and B are selected and jump 16 beats.\" data-iface=\"classic\"><span class=\"mf-spot\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span><div class=\"mf-marks\" role=\"group\" aria-label=\"Numbered points on the picture\"><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"1\" data-x=\"36.500\" data-y=\"14.583\" aria-label=\"1: PAGE 1\" aria-describedby=\"f-performance-2-1\">1<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"2\" data-x=\"51.000\" data-y=\"9.792\" aria-label=\"2: PAGE 2\" aria-describedby=\"f-performance-2-2\">2<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"3\" data-x=\"80.000\" data-y=\"9.792\" aria-label=\"3: PAGE 1: STOCK or MY SIZES\" aria-describedby=\"f-performance-2-3\">3<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"4\" data-x=\"31.375\" data-y=\"21.667\" aria-label=\"4: Pad pair\" aria-describedby=\"f-performance-2-4\">4<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"5\" data-x=\"28.500\" data-y=\"32.083\" aria-label=\"5: Beats\" aria-describedby=\"f-performance-2-5\">5<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"6\" data-x=\"28.500\" data-y=\"40.208\" aria-label=\"6: Bars\" aria-describedby=\"f-performance-2-6\">6<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"7\" data-x=\"91.875\" data-y=\"40.833\" aria-label=\"7: Readout\" aria-describedby=\"f-performance-2-7\">7<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"8\" data-x=\"21.500\" data-y=\"71.250\" aria-label=\"8: Sizes\" aria-describedby=\"f-performance-2-8\">8<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"9\" data-x=\"12.500\" data-y=\"88.542\" aria-label=\"9: Dock\" aria-describedby=\"f-performance-2-9\">9<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"10\" data-x=\"89.750\" data-y=\"88.542\" aria-label=\"10: Works on\" aria-describedby=\"f-performance-2-10\">10<\/button><\/div><\/div><\/div><figcaption>Editing page 2. Pads A and B are selected and jump 16 beats.<\/figcaption><ol class=\"mf-legend\" aria-label=\"What the numbers show\"><li data-n=\"1\" id=\"f-performance-2-1\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">1<\/span><div><b>PAGE 1<\/b> <span>Edit the sizes BEAT JUMP gives.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"2\" id=\"f-performance-2-2\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">2<\/span><div><b>PAGE 2<\/b> <span>Edit the sizes SHIFT + BEAT JUMP gives. The filled tab is the page you are editing.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"3\" id=\"f-performance-2-3\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">3<\/span><div><b>PAGE 1: STOCK or MY SIZES<\/b> <span>STOCK keeps the player's own 1, 2, 4 and 8 beats on page 1. MY SIZES uses yours. Page 2 always uses yours.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"4\" id=\"f-performance-2-4\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">4<\/span><div><b>Pad pair<\/b> <span>Two pads with one size. The left pad jumps back, the right pad forward. The selected pair has a light outline.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"5\" id=\"f-performance-2-5\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">5<\/span><div><b>Beats<\/b> <span>The size in beats.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"6\" id=\"f-performance-2-6\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">6<\/span><div><b>Bars<\/b> <span>The same size in bars. 4 beats make 1 bar.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"7\" id=\"f-performance-2-7\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">7<\/span><div><b>Readout<\/b> <span>The selected pair and its size.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"8\" id=\"f-performance-2-8\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">8<\/span><div><b>Sizes<\/b> <span>Tap a size to give it to the selected pair. The filled size is the current one.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"9\" id=\"f-performance-2-9\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">9<\/span><div><b>Dock<\/b> <span>What the highlighted control does.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"10\" id=\"f-performance-2-10\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">10<\/span><div><b>Works on<\/b> <span>Beat jump works on all four decks.<\/span><\/div><\/li><\/ol><\/figure>\n<ol class=\"steps\"><li>Choose PAGE 1 or PAGE 2.<\/li><li>For page 1, choose PAGE 1: MY SIZES. With STOCK, page 1 keeps the player's own sizes.<\/li><li>Tap a pad in the pair you want to change.<\/li><li>Tap a size in the row along the bottom.<\/li><\/ol>\n<p>Without the touch screen, turn the rotary selector to a pair, push it, then turn to step the size. It stops at the smallest and largest size. Push or press <span class=\"xzb\" data-key=\"back\"><img class=\"xzb-g\" src=\"assets/buttons/back.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"76.49\" height=\"32\"><span class=\"xzb-n\">BACK<\/span><\/span> when you are done.<\/p>\n<div class=\"table\"><table><thead><tr><th>Sizes you can choose<\/th><th><\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td>Beats<\/td><td>1, 2, 4, 8, 16, 32, 64, 128, 256<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Bars<\/td><td>1/4, 1/2, 1, 2, 4, 8, 16, 32, 64<\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div>\n<p>The sizes apply to every deck. UTILITY's own beat jump setting is separate and does not change them.<\/p>\n<div class=\"table\"><table><thead><tr><th>Setting<\/th><th>Choices<\/th><th>Default<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td>PAGE 1<\/td><td>STOCK, MY SIZES<\/td><td>MY SIZES<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Page 1 A/B, C/D, E/F, G/H<\/td><td>1 to 256 beats<\/td><td>1, 2, 4, 8 beats<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Page 2 A/B, C/D, E/F, G/H<\/td><td>1 to 256 beats<\/td><td>16, 32, 64, 128 beats<\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div>\n<h4 id=\"m-decks-3-and-4\" data-anchor=\"decks-3-and-4\">Decks 3 and 4<\/h4>\n<p>Decks 3 and 4 use the same sizes and both pages. They jump along the track's beat grid, or by its BPM when there is no grid. A track with neither jumps at 120 BPM, as on decks 1 and 2. With a loop on, the loop moves.<\/p>\n<h4 id=\"m-when-a-jump-is-refused\" data-anchor=\"when-a-jump-is-refused\">When a jump is refused<\/h4>\n<p>A jump the deck cannot make does nothing else. XZ Mods never silently shortens the selected distance. The screen shows why:<\/p>\n<div class=\"table\"><table><thead><tr><th>Notice<\/th><th>Deck<\/th><th>What it means<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td>JUMP UNAVAILABLE: TRACK EDGE, BUFFER OR DECK STATE<\/td><td>1 or 2<\/td><td>The player refused the jump. It would pass the start or end of the track, or the deck cannot jump right now.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>JUMP UNAVAILABLE: BEFORE TRACK START<\/td><td>3 or 4<\/td><td>The jump would land before the start of the track.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>JUMP UNAVAILABLE: AFTER TRACK END<\/td><td>3 or 4<\/td><td>The jump would land after the end of the track.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>JUMP UNAVAILABLE: LOOP MOVE OUT OF TRACK<\/td><td>3 or 4<\/td><td>Moving the loop would push it past the start or end.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>JUMP UNAVAILABLE: NO BEAT GRID OR BPM<\/td><td>3 or 4<\/td><td>The track's beat grid is damaged, so beats can't be counted. Analyse it in rekordbox again.<\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div>\n<h3 id=\"m-gate-cue-and-smart-cue\" data-anchor=\"gate-cue-and-smart-cue\">Gate cue and smart cue<\/h3>\n<p>Both change what a hot cue pad does in HOT CUE mode. Turn them on in MODS &gt; PLAY. Both are off by default, and each works on its own.<\/p>\n<div class=\"table\"><table><thead><tr><th>Feature<\/th><th>What a hot cue pad does<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td>GATE CUE<\/td><td>The track plays from the hot cue only while you hold the pad. Let go and it jumps back to the hot cue and pauses. Use it to stab hot cues like samples. Press <span class=\"xzb\" data-key=\"play-pause\"><img class=\"xzb-g\" src=\"assets/buttons/play-pause.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"133.62\" height=\"32\"><span class=\"xzb-n\">PLAY/PAUSE<\/span><\/span> while you hold the pad to keep playing after you let go.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>SMART CUE<\/td><td>Calling a hot cue also moves the CUE point there, so <span class=\"xzb\" data-key=\"cue\"><img class=\"xzb-g\" src=\"assets/buttons/cue.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"69.63\" height=\"32\"><span class=\"xzb-n\">CUE<\/span><\/span> takes you back to the last hot cue you used. Recording a new hot cue does not move it.<\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div>\n<p>Gate cue and smart cue work on all four decks. On decks 1 and 2 they need the cue engine; see below.<\/p>\n<h4 id=\"m-feature-setup\" data-anchor=\"feature-setup\">Feature setup<\/h4>\n<p>When the cue engine has not reported on a deck, MODS shows a short setup instead of the switch. It checks the feature on a loaded USB track in four steps: detect, choose deck, enable and test.<\/p>\n<figure class=\"mf\" id=\"f-performance-3\"><div class=\"mf-frame\"><div class=\"mf-bar\"><span class=\"mf-label\">MODS · FEATURE SETUP<\/span><\/div><div class=\"mf-stage\"><img src=\"manual/shots/9158cb8314079fb0.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"The setup page at its first step, checking gate cue. For smart cue it reads SMART CUE.\" data-iface=\"modern\"><img src=\"manual/shots/a62fe6fe88cc8161.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"The setup page at its first step, checking gate cue. For smart cue it reads SMART CUE.\" data-iface=\"classic\"><span class=\"mf-spot\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span><div class=\"mf-marks\" role=\"group\" aria-label=\"Numbered points on the picture\"><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"1\" data-x=\"33.750\" data-y=\"12.500\" aria-label=\"1: Feature\" aria-describedby=\"f-performance-3-1\">1<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"2\" data-x=\"48.750\" data-y=\"17.083\" aria-label=\"2: Steps\" aria-describedby=\"f-performance-3-2\">2<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"3\" data-x=\"51.250\" data-y=\"4.167\" aria-label=\"3: Deck\" aria-describedby=\"f-performance-3-3\">3<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"4\" data-x=\"46.875\" data-y=\"30.208\" aria-label=\"4: What to do\" aria-describedby=\"f-performance-3-4\">4<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"5\" data-x=\"49.375\" data-y=\"37.500\" aria-label=\"5: Track\" aria-describedby=\"f-performance-3-5\">5<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"6\" data-x=\"63.750\" data-y=\"43.542\" aria-label=\"6: Status\" aria-describedby=\"f-performance-3-6\">6<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"7\" data-x=\"38.750\" data-y=\"74.167\" aria-label=\"7: Next step\" aria-describedby=\"f-performance-3-7\">7<\/button><\/div><\/div><\/div><figcaption>The setup page at its first step, checking gate cue. For smart cue it reads SMART CUE.<\/figcaption><ol class=\"mf-legend\" aria-label=\"What the numbers show\"><li data-n=\"1\" id=\"f-performance-3-1\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">1<\/span><div><b>Feature<\/b> <span>The feature this setup checks.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"2\" id=\"f-performance-3-2\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">2<\/span><div><b>Steps<\/b> <span>The four steps. The button at the bottom always runs the next one.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"3\" id=\"f-performance-3-3\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">3<\/span><div><b>Deck<\/b> <span>Choose deck 1 or deck 2.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"4\" id=\"f-performance-3-4\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">4<\/span><div><b>What to do<\/b> <span>The instruction for the current step.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"5\" id=\"f-performance-3-5\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">5<\/span><div><b>Track<\/b> <span>The track loaded on the chosen deck.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"6\" id=\"f-performance-3-6\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">6<\/span><div><b>Status<\/b> <span>FEATURE DETECTED, or what to do when it is missing.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"7\" id=\"f-performance-3-7\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">7<\/span><div><b>Next step<\/b> <span>Runs the step. Missing support keeps its reason on the screen.<\/span><\/div><\/li><\/ol><\/figure>\n<ol class=\"steps\"><li>Load a track from USB on deck 1 or deck 2.<\/li><li>Press DETECT FEATURE.<\/li><li>Choose the deck, then enable the feature.<\/li><li>Close MODS and test it: hold and release a hot cue for gate cue, or call a hot cue and check that the cue point follows for smart cue.<\/li><li>Reopen the setup and confirm.<\/li><\/ol>\n<p>If the status still asks you to load a USB track while one is loaded, prepare the USB again with the current <a class=\"m-link\" href=\"#manual\" data-chapter=\"desktop-app\">XZ Mods app<\/a>.<\/p>\n<h3 id=\"m-keys-and-key-sync\" data-anchor=\"keys-and-key-sync\">Keys and KEY SYNC<\/h3>\n<p>XZ Mods can move the key of any deck a semitone at a time, and match a deck's key to the master deck with KEY SYNC. The master can be any deck, 1 to 4. The key display then shows the key the track plays in now.<\/p>\n<h4 id=\"m-from-the-deck\" data-anchor=\"from-the-deck\">From the deck<\/h4>\n<ol class=\"steps\"><li>Load tracks with analysed keys, and make the deck you want to match to the tempo master.<\/li><li>Hold <span class=\"xzb\" data-key=\"shift\"><img class=\"xzb-g\" src=\"assets/buttons/shift.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"57\" height=\"32\"><span class=\"xzb-n\">SHIFT<\/span><\/span> and press <span class=\"xzb\" data-key=\"sync\"><img class=\"xzb-g\" src=\"assets/buttons/sync.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"75.39\" height=\"32\"><span class=\"xzb-n\">SYNC<\/span><\/span> on the deck you want to move. On a side that drives deck 3 or 4, this moves that deck.<\/li><li>The deck shifts to a key that fits the master deck and MASTER TEMPO turns on. A notice shows the new key and the master deck, with RELATIVE KEY when it matches the relative major or minor.<\/li><\/ol>\n<p>To end KEY SYNC, press <span class=\"xzb\" data-key=\"shift\"><img class=\"xzb-g\" src=\"assets/buttons/shift.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"57\" height=\"32\"><span class=\"xzb-n\">SHIFT<\/span><\/span> + <span class=\"xzb\" data-key=\"sync\"><img class=\"xzb-g\" src=\"assets/buttons/sync.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"75.39\" height=\"32\"><span class=\"xzb-n\">SYNC<\/span><\/span> again, or press <span class=\"xzb\" data-key=\"master-tempo\"><img class=\"xzb-g\" src=\"assets/buttons/master-tempo.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"142.24\" height=\"32\"><span class=\"xzb-n\">MASTER TEMPO<\/span><\/span>. Both return the deck to its own key and put MASTER TEMPO back the way it was. After that, <span class=\"xzb\" data-key=\"master-tempo\"><img class=\"xzb-g\" src=\"assets/buttons/master-tempo.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"142.24\" height=\"32\"><span class=\"xzb-n\">MASTER TEMPO<\/span><\/span> works as on a stock player.<\/p>\n<p>KEY SYNC changes the key only. The tempo, SYNC and the master deck stay as they were.<\/p>\n<p>All four decks can hold key shifts and KEY SYNC together. Before starting a new shift on deck 3 or 4, the player checks its measured audio workload. If there is too little headroom, it shows <strong>KEY SHIFT REFUSED: AUDIO LOAD TOO HIGH<\/strong> and leaves the current keys unchanged. Shifts already in use keep running. SYSTEM READOUT shows render times and the number of active key shifters.<\/p>\n<p>If KEY SYNC cannot work, a notice or the deck's key display shows why for a few seconds:<\/p>\n<div class=\"table\"><table><thead><tr><th>Message<\/th><th>What to do<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td>KEY ENGINE OFF: SET UP KEYS<\/td><td>This USB loader has no key engine. Open MODS &gt; PLAY &gt; KEYS and press SET UP KEYS, or prepare the USB again with the current XZ Mods app.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>DECK 1 TRACK HAS NO KEY (or another deck)<\/td><td>The track on this deck has no analysed key. Analyse it in rekordbox.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>LOAD AN ANALYZED TRACK / SET UP KEYS<\/td><td>The deck has no track with an analysed key. Load one.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>LOAD A KEYED TRACK ON DECK 2 (or another deck)<\/td><td>The master deck has no track with an analysed key.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>THIS DECK IS MASTER, MAKE DECK 2 MASTER FIRST<\/td><td>The deck you pressed is the master, so there is nothing to match. Make another deck the master. On the KEYS page the master deck has no KEY SYNC button and says it is the master.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>SELECT ONE LOCAL MASTER / SET UP KEYS<\/td><td>No deck on this player is the tempo master. Press <span class=\"xzb\" data-key=\"master\"><img class=\"xzb-g\" src=\"assets/buttons/master.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"95.11\" height=\"32\"><span class=\"xzb-n\">MASTER<\/span><\/span> on the deck to match to.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>VERIFY MASTER PLAYING KEY / SET UP KEYS<\/td><td>The master deck's playing key is not known yet. Let it play a moment, then try again.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>MASTER CHANGED / RETRY KEY SYNC, TRACK CHANGED / RETRY KEY CONTROL<\/td><td>The master or the track changed before the key moved. Press again.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>KEY SHIFT REFUSED: AUDIO LOAD TOO HIGH<\/td><td>Measured audio work leaves too little headroom for a new shift. Existing shifts keep running. Check SYSTEM READOUT and retry when the load falls.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>SHIFT OUT OF RANGE, KEY RANGE IS -12 TO +12 SEMITONES<\/td><td>The key that fits is further away than the deck can shift.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>EMERGENCY LOOP / LOAD NEXT TRACK<\/td><td>The deck lost its track and loops. Load another track first.<\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div>\n<h4 id=\"m-the-keys-page\" data-anchor=\"the-keys-page\">The KEYS page<\/h4>\n<p>MODS &gt; PLAY &gt; KEYS does the same from the screen, and adds key shift by semitones. On the play screen, tapping a deck's key opens the same controls for that deck.<\/p>\n<figure class=\"mf\" id=\"f-performance-4\"><div class=\"mf-frame\"><div class=\"mf-bar\"><span class=\"mf-label\">MODS · KEYS<\/span><\/div><div class=\"mf-stage\"><img src=\"manual/shots/5aafe77c40783c50.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"The KEYS page for deck 1 with the key engine ready. The deck is in its own key.\" data-iface=\"modern\"><img src=\"manual/shots/615edda2b56db13d.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"The KEYS page for deck 1 with the key engine ready. The deck is in its own key.\" data-iface=\"classic\"><span class=\"mf-spot\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span><div class=\"mf-marks\" role=\"group\" aria-label=\"Numbered points on the picture\"><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"1\" data-x=\"30.250\" data-y=\"4.167\" aria-label=\"1: Deck\" aria-describedby=\"f-performance-4-1\">1<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"2\" data-x=\"24.625\" data-y=\"38.750\" aria-label=\"2: KEY DOWN\" aria-describedby=\"f-performance-4-2\">2<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"3\" data-x=\"41.625\" data-y=\"38.750\" aria-label=\"3: RESET\" aria-describedby=\"f-performance-4-3\">3<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"4\" data-x=\"58.875\" data-y=\"38.750\" aria-label=\"4: KEY UP\" aria-describedby=\"f-performance-4-4\">4<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"5\" data-x=\"82.500\" data-y=\"38.750\" aria-label=\"5: KEY SYNC\" aria-describedby=\"f-performance-4-5\">5<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"6\" data-x=\"37.500\" data-y=\"57.500\" aria-label=\"6: Deck keys\" aria-describedby=\"f-performance-4-6\">6<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"7\" data-x=\"89.750\" data-y=\"88.542\" aria-label=\"7: Works on\" aria-describedby=\"f-performance-4-7\">7<\/button><\/div><\/div><\/div><figcaption>The KEYS page for deck 1 with the key engine ready. The deck is in its own key.<\/figcaption><ol class=\"mf-legend\" aria-label=\"What the numbers show\"><li data-n=\"1\" id=\"f-performance-4-1\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">1<\/span><div><b>Deck<\/b> <span>Choose deck 1, 2, 3 or 4. Where there is room, a tab adds USB DECK for decks 1 and 2 and SOFTWARE for decks 3 and 4.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"2\" id=\"f-performance-4-2\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">2<\/span><div><b>KEY DOWN<\/b> <span>Lowers the deck's key one semitone.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"3\" id=\"f-performance-4-3\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">3<\/span><div><b>RESET<\/b> <span>Shows the current shift. Press it to return the deck to its own key.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"4\" id=\"f-performance-4-4\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">4<\/span><div><b>KEY UP<\/b> <span>Raises the deck's key one semitone.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"5\" id=\"f-performance-4-5\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">5<\/span><div><b>KEY SYNC<\/b> <span>Shifts the deck to a key that fits the master deck, as SHIFT + SYNC does.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"6\" id=\"f-performance-4-6\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">6<\/span><div><b>Deck keys<\/b> <span>Each deck's own key, the key it plays in now, the cents and SYNC or MASTER. The rows are empty in this picture.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"7\" id=\"f-performance-4-7\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">7<\/span><div><b>Works on<\/b> <span>Key shift and KEY SYNC work on all four decks.<\/span><\/div><\/li><\/ol><\/figure>\n<p>With MASTER TEMPO on, the key holds while the tempo moves. Without it, the tempo changes the key too, and the key display shows that.<\/p>\n<p>When the key engine has not reported, the buttons show an amber dot, the dock says NOT READY and <strong>SET UP KEYS<\/strong> appears. It opens a short setup that checks the key engine and the chosen deck's track, and ends with a live test:<\/p>\n<div class=\"mg\" id=\"f-performance-5\" data-iface=\"modern\"><figure class=\"mg-item\"><button class=\"mg-shot\" type=\"button\" data-zoom=\"manual/shots/78311cd25ed37802.webp\" data-w=\"800\" data-h=\"480\" aria-label=\"Enlarge: The KEYS page before the key engine reports, with SET UP KEYS\"><img src=\"manual/shots/78311cd25ed37802.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"><\/button><figcaption>The KEYS page before the key engine reports, with SET UP KEYS<\/figcaption><\/figure><\/div>\n<div class=\"mg\" id=\"f-performance-6\" data-iface=\"classic\"><figure class=\"mg-item\"><button class=\"mg-shot\" type=\"button\" data-zoom=\"manual/shots/3bcf0ff3a21f0598.webp\" data-w=\"800\" data-h=\"480\" aria-label=\"Enlarge: The KEYS page before the key engine reports, with SET UP KEYS\"><img src=\"manual/shots/3bcf0ff3a21f0598.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"><\/button><figcaption>The KEYS page before the key engine reports, with SET UP KEYS<\/figcaption><\/figure><\/div>\n<h4 id=\"m-the-key-on-the-modern-play-screen\" data-anchor=\"the-key-on-the-modern-play-screen\" data-iface=\"modern\">The key on the MODERN play screen <span class=\"tag tag--modern\">modern<\/span><\/h4>\n<p>In MODERN each deck's panel beside its waveform shows its key. With PLAYING KEY on, the big key is the key the track plays in now, after tempo and key shift.<\/p>\n<figure class=\"mf\" id=\"f-performance-7\"><div class=\"mf-frame\"><div class=\"mf-bar\"><span class=\"mf-label\">MODERN · KEY SYNC<\/span><\/div><div class=\"mf-stage\"><img src=\"manual/shots/c36b7163962dd08a.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"Deck 2 holds KEY SYNC: it plays Bb minor, moved up from its own A minor, 12 cents sharp.\"><span class=\"mf-spot\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span><div class=\"mf-marks\" role=\"group\" aria-label=\"Numbered points on the picture\"><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"1\" data-x=\"14.000\" data-y=\"41.667\" aria-label=\"1: Key panel\" aria-describedby=\"f-performance-7-1\">1<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"2\" data-x=\"14.000\" data-y=\"19.792\" aria-label=\"2: Deck in its own key\" aria-describedby=\"f-performance-7-2\">2<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"3\" data-x=\"76.500\" data-y=\"78.750\" aria-label=\"3: MT\" aria-describedby=\"f-performance-7-3\">3<\/button><\/div><\/div><\/div><figcaption>Deck 2 holds KEY SYNC: it plays Bb minor, moved up from its own A minor, 12 cents sharp.<\/figcaption><ol class=\"mf-legend\" aria-label=\"What the numbers show\"><li data-n=\"1\" id=\"f-performance-7-1\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">1<\/span><div><b>Key panel<\/b> <span>KEY SYNC, the key the deck plays in now, the cents left over and the track's own key.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"2\" id=\"f-performance-7-2\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">2<\/span><div><b>Deck in its own key<\/b> <span>Deck 1 plays in its own key, so the panel shows only KEY and the key.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"3\" id=\"f-performance-7-3\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">3<\/span><div><b>MT<\/b> <span>MASTER TEMPO. It blinks while KEY SYNC holds on that deck.<\/span><\/div><\/li><\/ol><\/figure>\n<div class=\"table\"><table><thead><tr><th>Part of the key panel<\/th><th>Meaning<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td>KEY SYNC<\/td><td>KEY SYNC holds on this deck.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>The big key<\/td><td>The key the deck plays in now. Green or amber compares it with the master deck's key; see <a class=\"m-link\" href=\"#manual\" data-chapter=\"play-screen\" data-anchor=\"key-and-key-sync\">Key and KEY SYNC<\/a>.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>+12¢<\/td><td>Cents between the playing key and the nearest semitone.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>ORIGINAL<\/td><td>The track's own key, shown when the playing key differs.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>▲1<\/td><td>The key shift in semitones, on older USB loaders that do not report the analysed key.<\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div>\n<div class=\"mg\" id=\"f-performance-8\" data-iface=\"modern\"><figure class=\"mg-item\"><button class=\"mg-shot\" type=\"button\" data-zoom=\"manual/shots/ba22f219e129ed1f.webp\" data-w=\"800\" data-h=\"480\" aria-label=\"Enlarge: KEY SYNC with the MT lamp in the dark half of its blink\"><img src=\"manual/shots/ba22f219e129ed1f.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"><\/button><figcaption>KEY SYNC with the MT lamp in the dark half of its blink<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class=\"mg-item\"><button class=\"mg-shot\" type=\"button\" data-zoom=\"manual/shots/b501a526a718aa04.webp\" data-w=\"800\" data-h=\"480\" aria-label=\"Enlarge: With MASTER TEMPO off, +2.20 % tempo lifts A minor by 38 cents\"><img src=\"manual/shots/b501a526a718aa04.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"><\/button><figcaption>With MASTER TEMPO off, +2.20 % tempo lifts A minor by 38 cents<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class=\"mg-item\"><button class=\"mg-shot\" type=\"button\" data-zoom=\"manual/shots/8fad872fc7559a67.webp\" data-w=\"800\" data-h=\"480\" aria-label=\"Enlarge: With MASTER TEMPO off and +6.10 % tempo, the track plays in Bb minor\"><img src=\"manual/shots/8fad872fc7559a67.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"><\/button><figcaption>With MASTER TEMPO off and +6.10 % tempo, the track plays in Bb minor<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class=\"mg-item\"><button class=\"mg-shot\" type=\"button\" data-zoom=\"manual/shots/543dad242d6f87b5.webp\" data-w=\"800\" data-h=\"480\" aria-label=\"Enlarge: Keys in WHEEL notation, deck 1 shifted down two semitones\"><img src=\"manual/shots/543dad242d6f87b5.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"><\/button><figcaption>Keys in WHEEL notation, deck 1 shifted down two semitones<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class=\"mg-item\"><button class=\"mg-shot\" type=\"button\" data-zoom=\"manual/shots/6006460a8c5e74a9.webp\" data-w=\"800\" data-h=\"480\" aria-label=\"Enlarge: An older USB loader shows the key and its shift step only\"><img src=\"manual/shots/6006460a8c5e74a9.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"><\/button><figcaption>An older USB loader shows the key and its shift step only<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class=\"mg-item\"><button class=\"mg-shot\" type=\"button\" data-zoom=\"manual/shots/d088e6ddb1537187.webp\" data-w=\"800\" data-h=\"480\" aria-label=\"Enlarge: No key on deck 1, and a key name too long for the panel\"><img src=\"manual/shots/d088e6ddb1537187.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"><\/button><figcaption>No key on deck 1, and a key name too long for the panel<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class=\"mg-item\"><button class=\"mg-shot\" type=\"button\" data-zoom=\"manual/shots/f9b6997b34a4582c.webp\" data-w=\"800\" data-h=\"480\" aria-label=\"Enlarge: The top bar lamps and QUANTIZE lamps hidden\"><img src=\"manual/shots/f9b6997b34a4582c.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"><\/button><figcaption>The top bar lamps and QUANTIZE lamps hidden<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class=\"mg-item\"><button class=\"mg-shot\" type=\"button\" data-zoom=\"manual/shots/fa14e55f7a57bdb1.webp\" data-w=\"800\" data-h=\"480\" aria-label=\"Enlarge: The same, with BEAT FX on\"><img src=\"manual/shots/fa14e55f7a57bdb1.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"><\/button><figcaption>The same, with BEAT FX on<\/figcaption><\/figure><\/div>\n<h4 id=\"m-the-key-on-the-classic-play-screen\" data-anchor=\"the-key-on-the-classic-play-screen\" data-iface=\"classic\">The key on the CLASSIC play screen <span class=\"tag tag--classic\">classic<\/span><\/h4>\n<p>In CLASSIC, XZ Mods draws the playing key where the player shows its beat countdown, under the key:<\/p>\n<div class=\"table\"><table><thead><tr><th>What you see<\/th><th>Meaning<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td>KEY and a key<\/td><td>The track plays in its own key.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>TRACK KEY<\/td><td>Deck 3 or 4 shows the track's own key until it reports the key it plays in.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Own key ▸ playing key<\/td><td>The tempo or a key shift moved the key.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>SYNC<\/td><td>KEY SYNC holds on this deck. The tile turns green while the key matches the master.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>MASTER<\/td><td>This deck is the master that KEY SYNC matches to.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>+12c in amber<\/td><td>Cents between the playing key and the nearest semitone.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Green or amber key<\/td><td>The playing key compared with the master deck's key, as KEY MATCH COLOURS sets it.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>A message in red<\/td><td>KEY SYNC could not work; see the table above.<\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div>\n<h4 id=\"m-playing-key\" data-anchor=\"playing-key\">PLAYING KEY<\/h4>\n<p>PLAYING KEY is on by default. Turn it off in MODS &gt; SCREEN to show the track's own key instead. In CLASSIC, off brings the beat countdown back. Key notation (AS ON THE USB, MUSICAL or WHEEL) is set on the same page; see <a class=\"m-link\" href=\"#manual\" data-chapter=\"screen-and-themes\">Screen, interfaces and themes<\/a>.<\/p>\n<p>Decks 3 and 4 show their playing key too, after tempo and key shift. Until a software deck reports it, the deck shows the track's own key.<\/p>\n<h3 id=\"m-ram-tracks\" data-anchor=\"ram-tracks\">RAM tracks <span class=\"tag tag--experimental\">experimental<\/span><\/h3>\n<p>RAM TRACKS copies the track on a deck into the player's memory. The deck then plays from memory, so it keeps playing if the music USB goes out. It works on all four decks. Decks 3 and 4 need the loopback cable connected to start a copy.<\/p>\n<figure class=\"mf\" id=\"f-performance-9\"><div class=\"mf-frame\"><div class=\"mf-bar\"><span class=\"mf-label\">MODS · RAM TRACKS<\/span><\/div><div class=\"mf-stage\"><img src=\"manual/shots/95dd0042df78e900.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"Deck 1 on a USB loader without the RAM engine.\" data-iface=\"modern\"><img src=\"manual/shots/7991b8883b02c664.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"Deck 1 on a USB loader without the RAM engine.\" data-iface=\"classic\"><span class=\"mf-spot\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span><div class=\"mf-marks\" role=\"group\" aria-label=\"Numbered points on the picture\"><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"1\" data-x=\"30.000\" data-y=\"24.167\" aria-label=\"1: Deck\" aria-describedby=\"f-performance-9-1\">1<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"2\" data-x=\"56.250\" data-y=\"32.292\" aria-label=\"2: State\" aria-describedby=\"f-performance-9-2\">2<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"3\" data-x=\"44.750\" data-y=\"37.500\" aria-label=\"3: Source\" aria-describedby=\"f-performance-9-3\">3<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"4\" data-x=\"73.750\" data-y=\"45.417\" aria-label=\"4: Progress\" aria-describedby=\"f-performance-9-4\">4<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"5\" data-x=\"46.875\" data-y=\"50.417\" aria-label=\"5: Memory\" aria-describedby=\"f-performance-9-5\">5<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"6\" data-x=\"41.250\" data-y=\"64.167\" aria-label=\"6: Action\" aria-describedby=\"f-performance-9-6\">6<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"7\" data-x=\"40.625\" data-y=\"73.958\" aria-label=\"7: Scope\" aria-describedby=\"f-performance-9-7\">7<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"8\" data-x=\"68.500\" data-y=\"94.167\" aria-label=\"8: Reason\" aria-describedby=\"f-performance-9-8\">8<\/button><\/div><\/div><\/div><figcaption>Deck 1 on a USB loader without the RAM engine.<\/figcaption><ol class=\"mf-legend\" aria-label=\"What the numbers show\"><li data-n=\"1\" id=\"f-performance-9-1\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">1<\/span><div><b>Deck<\/b> <span>Choose deck 1, 2, 3 or 4.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"2\" id=\"f-performance-9-2\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">2<\/span><div><b>State<\/b> <span>The deck and the state of its RAM copy.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"3\" id=\"f-performance-9-3\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">3<\/span><div><b>Source<\/b> <span>The track loaded on that deck, or what to do next.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"4\" id=\"f-performance-9-4\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">4<\/span><div><b>Progress<\/b> <span>How much of the track is copied, in MiB.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"5\" id=\"f-performance-9-5\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">5<\/span><div><b>Memory<\/b> <span>How much of the 128 MiB the copies use, prepared stems apart, then each deck's copy and state.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"6\" id=\"f-performance-9-6\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">6<\/span><div><b>Action<\/b> <span>The one next step for this state: set up, choose a track, load, cancel, retry or release.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"7\" id=\"f-performance-9-7\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">7<\/span><div><b>Scope<\/b> <span>What RAM holds for this deck. COPIES AUDIO / STEMS STAY ON USB means only the original audio goes into RAM.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"8\" id=\"f-performance-9-8\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">8<\/span><div><b>Reason<\/b> <span>Why the feature is not available. Here the RAM engine is missing.<\/span><\/div><\/li><\/ol><\/figure>\n<ol class=\"steps\"><li>Load a track from USB on the deck.<\/li><li>Open MODS &gt; PLAY &gt; RAM TRACKS and choose that deck.<\/li><li>Press LOAD TRACK INTO RAM. Keep the USB connected while it copies.<\/li><li>Wait for ORIGINAL AUDIO IN RAM.<\/li><\/ol>\n<p>A track that plays is also copied on its own when there is room. CANCEL COPY or RELEASE RAM COPY stops that for the loaded track.<\/p>\n<div class=\"table\"><table><thead><tr><th>State<\/th><th>Button<\/th><th>What it means<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td>RAM ENGINE NOT DETECTED<\/td><td>SET UP RAM TRACKS<\/td><td>This USB loader has no RAM engine, or it has not reported yet. The setup checks the engine. If it stays, prepare the USB again with the current XZ Mods app.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>LOOPBACK CABLE NOT CONNECTED<\/td><td>SET UP FOUR DECKS<\/td><td>Deck 3 or 4 is chosen and decks 3 and 4 are not running. The button opens 4 DECKS.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>NOT IN RAM<\/td><td>LOAD TRACK INTO RAM<\/td><td>The deck plays from USB.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>COPYING TO RAM<\/td><td>CANCEL COPY<\/td><td>The copy is running. Cancel leaves the track playing from USB.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>ORIGINAL AUDIO IN RAM<\/td><td>RELEASE RAM COPY<\/td><td>The deck plays from memory. Release frees the memory and needs the USB still connected.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>COPY FAILED<\/td><td>RETRY LOAD INTO RAM<\/td><td>The track keeps playing from USB. Retry; if it fails again, load the track again from USB.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>USB OUT / RAM COPY ONLY<\/td><td>BACK TO PLAY<\/td><td>The USB is out and the deck plays from memory. The play screen says so in the deck's lane; see <a class=\"m-link\" href=\"#manual\" data-chapter=\"performance\" data-anchor=\"when-the-music-usb-goes-out\">below<\/a>. Load another track to release the copy.<\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div>\n<p>When a copy does not fit, the page says why and offers the next step:<\/p>\n<div class=\"table\"><table><thead><tr><th>Message<\/th><th>What to do<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td>This file exceeds the 64 MiB RAM limit.<\/td><td>Press CHOOSE ANOTHER TRACK.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Other RAM tracks leave too little space for this file.<\/td><td>Press MANAGE RAM TRACKS, choose a deck with a copy and release it.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Free RAM cannot keep the 64 MiB safety reserve.<\/td><td>Release another copy the same way.<\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div>\n<ul><li>One track per deck. Each file can be up to 64 MiB, and all four decks together up to 128 MiB. The player always keeps 64 MiB of its memory free.<\/li><li>RAM TRACKS copies the original audio. On decks 1 and 2, the line under the action button says what else is held; see the table below.<\/li><li>On decks 3 and 4 the waveform, beat grid and cues already loaded stay with the copy when the USB goes out. Cues you change then are kept for the session and not written to a USB.<\/li><li>If the loopback cable goes out, decks 3 and 4 keep their copies and pause, as they do without RAM. They do not start again on their own when the cable returns.<\/li><li>Loading another track on the deck drops its RAM copy.<\/li><\/ul>\n<h4 id=\"m-when-the-music-usb-goes-out\" data-anchor=\"when-the-music-usb-goes-out\">When the music USB goes out <span class=\"tag tag--experimental\">experimental<\/span><\/h4>\n<div class=\"mx\" data-mx=\"ram-usb\" data-mode=\"scenes\" role=\"group\" aria-label=\"A deck playing from RAM when the USB goes out\"><ol class=\"mx-scenes\"><li data-title=\"NOT IN RAM\"><b>NOT IN RAM<\/b> <span>The deck plays from USB.<\/span><\/li><li data-title=\"COPYING TO RAM\"><b>COPYING TO RAM<\/b> <span>Press LOAD TRACK INTO RAM. Keep the USB connected while it copies.<\/span><\/li><li data-title=\"ORIGINAL AUDIO IN RAM\"><b>ORIGINAL AUDIO IN RAM<\/b> <span>The deck plays from memory.<\/span><\/li><li data-title=\"USB OUT / RAM COPY ONLY\"><b>USB OUT / RAM COPY ONLY<\/b> <span>The music USB goes out and the deck plays on from memory. A teal card, WHOLE TRACK IN RAM · PLAYABLE, takes the waveform's place and says how to get it back.<\/span><\/li><\/ol><\/div>\n<p>A deck with its whole track in RAM keeps playing when the music USB goes out. The waveform was read from the USB, so the deck's lane cannot draw it any more. A teal card takes its place: <strong>WHOLE TRACK IN RAM · PLAYABLE<\/strong>, and under it how to get the waveform back.<\/p>\n<p>Everything else about the deck stays on screen: title and artist, time and remain, BPM, tempo, key, the lamps, the hot cues and the playhead.<\/p>\n<div class=\"mg\" id=\"f-performance-10\" data-iface=\"modern\"><figure class=\"mg-item\"><button class=\"mg-shot\" type=\"button\" data-zoom=\"manual/shots/1a547fb24d2e757b.webp\" data-w=\"800\" data-h=\"480\" aria-label=\"Enlarge: 2 DECKS: deck 1 plays from RAM. Deck 2 is unchanged\"><img src=\"manual/shots/1a547fb24d2e757b.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"><\/button><figcaption>2 DECKS: deck 1 plays from RAM. Deck 2 is unchanged<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class=\"mg-item\"><button class=\"mg-shot\" type=\"button\" data-zoom=\"manual/shots/ffa2833cdc0d684b.webp\" data-w=\"800\" data-h=\"480\" aria-label=\"Enlarge: Both decks play from RAM\"><img src=\"manual/shots/ffa2833cdc0d684b.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"><\/button><figcaption>Both decks play from RAM<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class=\"mg-item\"><button class=\"mg-shot\" type=\"button\" data-zoom=\"manual/shots/3aa1f0dd34a998f9.webp\" data-w=\"800\" data-h=\"480\" aria-label=\"Enlarge: 4 DECKS: decks 2 and 4 play from RAM\"><img src=\"manual/shots/3aa1f0dd34a998f9.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"><\/button><figcaption>4 DECKS: decks 2 and 4 play from RAM<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class=\"mg-item\"><button class=\"mg-shot\" type=\"button\" data-zoom=\"manual/shots/dc04753cbaf97061.webp\" data-w=\"800\" data-h=\"480\" aria-label=\"Enlarge: MIXER order: the card stays with its deck\"><img src=\"manual/shots/dc04753cbaf97061.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"><\/button><figcaption>MIXER order: the card stays with its deck<\/figcaption><\/figure><\/div>\n<figure class=\"mf\" id=\"f-performance-11\" data-iface=\"classic\"><div class=\"mf-frame\"><div class=\"mf-bar\"><span class=\"mf-label\">PLAY · CLASSIC<\/span><\/div><div class=\"mf-stage\"><img src=\"manual/shots/247996364f4e6968.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"Deck 1 plays from RAM after the USB went out. The stem rows, the deck column and the deck strip stay as the player shows them.\"><span class=\"mf-spot\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span><div class=\"mf-marks\" role=\"group\" aria-label=\"Numbered points on the picture\"><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"1\" data-x=\"80.000\" data-y=\"15.000\" aria-label=\"1: RAM card\" aria-describedby=\"f-performance-11-1\">1<\/button><\/div><\/div><\/div><figcaption>Deck 1 plays from RAM after the USB went out. The stem rows, the deck column and the deck strip stay as the player shows them.<\/figcaption><ol class=\"mf-legend\" aria-label=\"What the numbers show\"><li data-n=\"1\" id=\"f-performance-11-1\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">1<\/span><div><b>RAM card<\/b> <span>The deck plays its whole track from RAM. The second line says how to get the waveform back.<\/span><\/div><\/li><\/ol><\/figure>\n<p>To get the waveform back, reinsert the same USB or insert another, then load a track from it. The card goes as soon as the deck has a waveform to draw again. Loading a track also ends the deck's RAM copy, as it always does.<\/p>\n<p>On decks 3 and 4 the waveform loaded before the USB went out stays, so the card shows there only if the waveform had not loaded yet.<\/p>\n<div class=\"table\"><table><thead><tr><th>Line under the button, decks 1 and 2<\/th><th>What it means<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td>COPIES AUDIO / STEMS STAY ON USB<\/td><td>No copy yet. RAM TRACKS copies the audio, not the stems.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>AUDIO IN RAM / STEMS NEED USB<\/td><td>The audio is in RAM. The stems still read the USB.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>AUDIO + STEMS IN RAM / WAVES KEPT<\/td><td>The deck's prepared stems are held in RAM as well, and the loaded waveforms stay.<\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div>\n<aside class=\"callout callout--experimental\"><b>Experimental<\/b><p>Playing on from RAM after the USB goes out has not been confirmed on a player yet. Keep the USB in during a set.<\/p><\/aside>\n<h3 id=\"m-quantize\" data-anchor=\"quantize\">Quantize<\/h3>\n<p>On decks 1 and 2, quantize is the player's own: <span class=\"xzb\" data-key=\"deck-quantize\"><img class=\"xzb-g\" src=\"assets/buttons/deck-quantize.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"144.23\" height=\"32\"><span class=\"xzb-n\">DECK QUANTIZE<\/span><\/span> and UTILITY work as on a stock player. In MODERN each deck shows its QUANTIZE lamp and beat value above its time. You can hide them in MODS &gt; SCREEN &gt; LAMPS AND TITLES.<\/p>\n<p>While a side drives deck 3 or 4:<\/p>\n<div class=\"table\"><table><thead><tr><th>Key<\/th><th>Action<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td><span class=\"xzb\" data-key=\"deck-quantize\"><img class=\"xzb-g\" src=\"assets/buttons/deck-quantize.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"144.23\" height=\"32\"><span class=\"xzb-n\">DECK QUANTIZE<\/span><\/span><\/td><td>Switches quantize for every deck. Decks 1 and 2 switch through the player as before.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td><span class=\"xzb\" data-key=\"shift\"><img class=\"xzb-g\" src=\"assets/buttons/shift.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"57\" height=\"32\"><span class=\"xzb-n\">SHIFT<\/span><\/span> + <span class=\"xzb\" data-key=\"deck-quantize\"><img class=\"xzb-g\" src=\"assets/buttons/deck-quantize.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"144.23\" height=\"32\"><span class=\"xzb-n\">DECK QUANTIZE<\/span><\/span><\/td><td>Switches quantize only for the deck of that side.<\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div>\n<p>With quantize on, decks 3 and 4 put cue points, loop in and out, hot cues and beat and slip loops on the beat grid, at a one-beat value. <span class=\"xzb\" data-key=\"sync\"><img class=\"xzb-g\" src=\"assets/buttons/sync.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"75.39\" height=\"32\"><span class=\"xzb-n\">SYNC<\/span><\/span> then also locks the deck to the master's beat. <a class=\"m-link\" href=\"#manual\" data-chapter=\"four-decks\">Four decks<\/a> has the rest of what decks 3 and 4 do.<\/p>";
